-- The Hexagonal Chest event (Kiciamol, 14 October): a person's Metin stone
-- may drop the hexagonal chest of the map it was broken on while the panel's
-- /events page runs the event. The rules - the map table, the panel's file,
-- the chance, the windows, who gets nothing - are m2_hexagonal_event.lua's,
-- a library the quest libraries load (tests/quest_hexagonal_event_test.sh).
-- The login starts each core's five-second clock, which writes the core's
-- answer for the panel; the kill reads the panel's file when it is due.
quest hexagonal_event begin
	state start begin
		when login begin
			m2_hex_event.start_clock()
		end
		when hexagonal_event_tick.server_timer begin
			m2_hex_event.refresh(false)
		end
		-- npc.is_pc() first: npc.get_type() reads the victim's mob table, which a
		-- character has none of, and a player killed in PvP took the core down
		-- (m2zip, 14 October).
		when kill with not npc.is_pc() and npc.get_type() == 2 begin
			m2_hex_event.kill()
		end
	end
end
